# Animations

## Library

Use **Framer Motion** only. No GSAP-heavy architecture or duplicate animation libraries.

## Philosophy

Enhance UX and emotional storytelling; never reduce usability, hurt performance, distract, or block interaction. Subtle > flashy.

## Style

Soft, cinematic, elegant, lightweight, natural. Avoid aggressive motion, excessive bounce, exaggerated scale, chaotic transitions.

## Durations

| Use | Range |
|-----|-------|
| Fast interactions | 100–200ms |
| Standard UI | 200–400ms |
| Cinematic reveals | 400–700ms |
| **Max** | 800ms |

## Easing

Prefer `ease-out` and smooth cubic-bezier. Avoid linear or over-bouncy easing.

## Properties

Animate **`transform`** and **`opacity`** only on mobile. Avoid heavy blur, large animated shadows, parallax spam.

## Scroll

Lightweight viewport reveals; no scroll-jacking, excessive parallax, or animation on every section.

## Hover

Subtle scale/opacity/elevation — remember mobile has no hover.

## Loading

Skeleton loaders, subtle shimmer, soft fades — not aggressive spinners.

## Modals

Fade + slight scale or slide; quick appearance; no dramatic zooms.

## Editor

Responsive and instant — no animation lag during typing/editing.

## Public Invitations

Cinematic reveals OK; performance still #1. Not an animation showcase.

### Royal template cinematic kit (`src/templates/royal/components/`)

| Component | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| `CinematicIntro` | Curtain split on tap; once per session (`sessionStorage`); skip when `isPreview` or reduced motion |
| `WeddingDateScratchReveal` | Magic UI `ScratchToReveal` on hero date; touch/pointer; skip when reduced motion |
| `SparkleOverlay` | CSS `@keyframes` particles (`transform`/`opacity` only) |

Use `usePrefersReducedMotion` from `src/templates/royal/hooks/`. No infinite JS animation loops.

## Reduced Motion

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; degrade gracefully on low-end devices.

## Priority

1. performance 2. usability 3. smoothness 4. elegance 5. subtlety
